10
01:14:26,666 --> 01:14:32,666
Race is a 2016 biographical sports drama film about African-American athlete Jesse Owens,
who won a record-breaking four gold medals at the 1936 Berlin Olympic Games.

11
01:21:53,333 --> 01:21:59,333
Directed by Stephen Hopkins and written by Joe Shrapnel and Anna Waterhouse, the film stars Stephan James
as Owens, and co-stars Jason Sudeikis, Jeremy Irons, William Hurt and Carice van Houten.

12
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:26,000
It is a co-production of Canada, Germany and France.

13
01:36:46,666 --> 01:36:52,666
Principal photography began on 24 July 2014, in Montreal, Canada.

14
01:44:13,333 --> 01:44:19,333
Forecast Pictures, Solofilms and Trinity Race produced the film, supported by the Owens
family, the Jesse Owens Foundation, the Jesse Owens Trust and the Luminary Group.

15
01:51:40,000 --> 01:51:46,000
The film was a commercial success and received mixed to positive reviews,
winning four Canadian Screen Awards, including Best Actor for James.

16
01:59:06,666 --> 01:59:12,666
The film explores themes of berlin, germany, sports,
olympic games, biography, historical figure.

17
02:06:33,333 --> 02:06:39,333
The tone is emotional.
